This is a specific cell culture passaging protocol with particular constraints (one biosafety cabinet, sequential flask processing, resource sharing). It's unlikely to be in the public catalog, so I'll author it from the source text.

**Analysis of the workflow:**

- **Tracks needed:** One main track for Flask A, one for Flask B (Flask B queues for the cabinet and centrifuge), one for finishing.
- **Key constraints:** 
  - Biosafety cabinet (one at a time; Flask A and B queue)
  - 37°C water bath (pre-warming; assumed unlimited)
  - CO₂ incubator (two flasks in parallel; enough capacity)
  - Benchtop centrifuge (one at a time; Flask A, then Flask B)
  - Microscope with haemocytometer (one at a time; Flask A, then Flask B)
  - One operator (all work is sequential across the two flasks)

- **Cabinet contention:** Flask A uses it in steps 3, 5, 9; Flask B uses it in steps 11, 13, 17. Flask B waits for Flask A to finish each cabinet phase.
- **Centrifuge contention:** Flask A step 6, then Flask B step 14.
- **Microscope contention:** Flask A step 8, then Flask B step 16.
- **Incubator:** Both flasks in parallel; no constraint (large capacity).

